{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This is the matter that HaShem commanded.</b> When He said at Mount Sinai, וְלֹא תִשָּׁבְעוּ בִשְׁמִי לַשֶּׁקֶר וְחִלַּלְתָּ (Leviticus 19:12), the intent was 'a man who vows or swears shall not break his word,' for by breaking his word he profanes HaShem. But a woman who is not under her own authority does not profane [it] if the one who annuls [her vow] renders it void."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:19.143115440Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}